# MachFive OAuth 2.0 Implementation — Complete Guide

There are **4 phases**: Supabase config, consent screen UI, MCP server code update, and testing. This is confirmed against Anthropic's Connectors FAQ, Supabase's OAuth Server docs, and FastMCP's `SupabaseProvider` source.

---

## Phase 1 — Configure Supabase OAuth Server

**Step 1.1 — Switch JWT signing to RS256**

Supabase defaults to HS256 (symmetric). OAuth requires asymmetric keys so clients can validate tokens without your secret.

1. Go to your Supabase dashboard → **Authentication** → **Signing Keys** (under JSON Web Tokens)
2. Generate a new RS256 or ES256 key
3. Set it as the active signing key
4. ⚠️ This changes how all JWTs are signed — make sure your existing app's token validation isn't hardcoded to HS256 before doing this

**Step 1.2 — Enable the OAuth Server**

1. Go to **Authentication** → **OAuth Server** in the sidebar
2. Toggle **"Enable OAuth server functionality"** on
3. Set the **Authorization Path** to `/oauth/consent`
   - Your Site URL is `https://app.machfive.co` (from **Authentication** → **URL Configuration**)
   - This means the full consent screen URL will be `https://app.machfive.co/oauth/consent`
4. Enable **Dynamic Client Registration** — this lets Claude.ai register itself automatically without you needing to pre-register it

Once enabled, Supabase exposes these endpoints automatically (replace `<project-ref>` with your actual Supabase project ref):

```
Authorization:  https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/oauth/authorize
Token:          https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/oauth/token
JWKS:           https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/auth/v1/.well-known/jwks.json
Discovery:      https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server/auth/v1
```

MCP clients like Claude.ai will **auto-discover** all of this from the discovery URL — you don't have to configure anything on their end.

